<onlyinclude>'''Power electronics''' is the technology that changes electrical energy into the form a device needs. It can turn wall-outlet AC into DC for electronics, raise or lower a battery voltage, or produce AC for an electric motor.</onlyinclude>

== How it works ==
Rather than waste excess voltage as heat, many converters turn semiconductor switches on and off rapidly. Coils and capacitors temporarily store energy and smooth the output. A controller adjusts switching to meet the desired voltage or current.

== Everyday examples ==
* A phone charger converts mains electricity into a controlled DC output.
* An electric-vehicle inverter supplies a motor from a battery.
* A solar inverter converts panel output for use by AC equipment.

== Why design matters ==
No converter is perfectly efficient: some energy becomes heat. Fast switching can also produce electrical noise. Designers choose suitable switches, cooling, protective circuits and isolation for the intended voltage and environment.

